# SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000059  -  CAT II
# The web server must produce log records containing sufficient information
# to establish the source of events.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000059
group:           V-206362
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-000133
control_rev5:    AU-3

contribution:    Splunk's web access logs record the client address of every request. The
                 application controls that those logs are written and that no REST endpoint
                 is excluded from them; where a reverse proxy fronts the instance,
                 tools.proxy.on makes all of its HTTP services take the client address from
                 the X-Forwarded-* headers instead of the proxy's own.

governs:         restmap.conf - The management interface endpoints, and which clients may reach them.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           restmap.conf [<rest endpoint name>:<endpoint description string>] includeInAccessLog not_equals false
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] log.access_file https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] log.access_file non_empty
                 reason: "log.access_file = <filename>. The HTTP access log filename. This
                         file is written in the default $SPLUNK_HOME/var/log directory.
                         Default: web_access.log" Related shipped settings:
                         log.access_maxsize = 25000000 and log.access_maxfiles = 5.
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Where a proxy or load balancer fronts the instance, the client address
                 must be inserted by that device in X-Forwarded-For; that case and the
                 matching tools.proxy settings are assessed under
                 SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000060.
external:        The source address field is emitted by the product in a fixed record
                 format with no configuration surface.

citation:        SRG-APP-000098-WSR-000059 check text; web.conf.spec:871-874
                 (log.access_file = <filename>, Default: web_access.log), :797-804
                 (trustedIP = <ip_addresses>), :1016-1033 (tools.proxy.on = <boolean>,
                 Default: false; tools.proxy.base = <scheme>://<URL>, Default: empty
                 string); restmap.conf.spec:138-142 (includeInAccessLog = <boolean>,
                 Default: true)
finding:         Splunk Enterprise has no web access log configured, or excludes REST
                 endpoints from splunkd_access.log, so the records available do not
                 establish the source of web events.
